-- title:
--   Nonzero level-N form with prescribed T_ℓ and U_q eigenvalues
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number such that no prime cube divides $N$, let $M_g$ be a nonzero divisor of $N$, and let $g$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project: $g$ is a normalized eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients, $a_n(g)$ being the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$ with respect to width $1$, satisfy $a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, the recursion $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)-p\,a_{p^r}(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M_g$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)$ for primes $p\mid M_g$), and for no proper divisor $M$ of $M_g$ does there exist a normalized eigenform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose coefficients at primes not dividing $M_g$ agree with those of $g$. Assume further that every prime $q$ with $q\mid N$ and $q^2\nmid N$ divides $M_g$, and that $a_q(g)=0$ for every prime $q$ with $q^2\mid M_g$. Then there is a nonzero weight-$2$ cusp form $g'$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ such that, writing $T_\ell$ and $U_q$ for the linear operators on cusp forms given by $f\mapsto\sum_{j<\ell}f\mid[2]\,$`heckeMatrix`$\,\ell\,j+f\mid[2]\,$`heckeDiagMatrix`$\,\ell$ and $f\mapsto\sum_{j<q}f\mid[2]\,$`heckeMatrix`$\,q\,j$ respectively: $T_\ell g'=a_\ell(g)\,g'$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N$; $U_q g'=0$ for every prime $q$ with $q^2\mid N$; and $U_q g'=a_q(g)\,g'$ for every prime $q$ with $q\mid N$ and $q^2\nmid N$.
--
--   This is the construction of the distinguished line in the oldspace of a newform $g$ on which the algebra generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell\nmid N$) and the $U_q$ ($q\mid N$) acts through the prescribed characters — the $\mathbb{T}_\Sigma$-eigenform at level $N$ attached to $g$, with $U_q$ acting by $0$ at primes exactly dividing $N$ to order at least two. It is used in the construction of a suitable subfamily and idempotent splitting at an auxiliary level in the local study of the Hecke action.
